# Map every commit written under the placeholder identity onto the real one.
#
# 97 early commits were authored as "lucin <lucin@example.com>" - the local
# machine's account name against example.com, the domain RFC 2606 reserves for
# documentation. That made `git shortlog` and the GitHub contributor list show
# two authors for one person, and gave the placeholder address a permanent,
# publicly visible record in the history.
#
# A mailmap is the fix that needs no history rewrite: git rewrites the display
# for any commit whose identity matches the left-hand side, while the objects
# and their hashes stay exactly as they are. Force-pushing 97 rewritten commits
# would change every hash after the earliest one and would invalidate every
# clone and open pull request, so it is not worth it for a cosmetic problem.
#
# Format: Proper Name <proper@email> <commit@email>
lucindie09-boop <lucindie09@gmail.com> lucin <lucin@example.com>
